WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.400
A Venus flytrap has no brain.

2
00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:04.900
Yet a touch can leave
a fading memory.

3
00:00:05.267 --> 00:00:07.333
A brief bend of a sensitive hair

4
00:00:07.333 --> 00:00:09.300
can send an electrical signal

5
00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:11.733
through the trap
while it stays open.

6
00:00:12.333 --> 00:00:13.967
Alongside that signal,

7
00:00:13.967 --> 00:00:16.800
calcium rises
inside the leaf’s cells.

8
00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:19.000
Then the calcium level falls.

9
00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:20.333
For a short time,

10
00:00:20.333 --> 00:00:22.267
part of that change remains.

11
00:00:22.967 --> 00:00:25.700
Another signal arriving
soon enough

12
00:00:25.700 --> 00:00:27.067
raises the level further.

13
00:00:27.067 --> 00:00:29.500
If it reaches the level
needed for closure,

14
00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:31.267
the trap can snap shut.

15
00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:33.133
Wait too long,

16
00:00:33.133 --> 00:00:34.300
and the next signal

17
00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:36.367
may no longer reach that level.

18
00:00:37.067 --> 00:00:39.633
Two signals don’t always
mean two touches:

19
00:00:39.633 --> 00:00:41.633
one slower hair movement

20
00:00:41.633 --> 00:00:42.733
can produce both.

21
00:00:43.333 --> 00:00:45.867
Here, memory means
retained information

22
00:00:45.867 --> 00:00:47.767
a fading chemical state,

23
00:00:47.767 --> 00:00:49.867
not conscious recollection.
